    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters July 6th with **James Wood** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting a massive 78.27 score, **James Wood** draws a favorable matchup against Burrows and his 4.71 xERA; the combination of a leadoff spot and elite 0.425 xwOBA makes him an auto-start. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** (73.02) and **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) provide the high-floor production we need. **Corbin Carroll** maintains a strong outlook despite the park factor drag against Walker Buehler, while **Isaac Paredes** benefits significantly from a 14% skill adjustment against Mikolas, who struggles to suppress hard contact in the specific environment we are targeting today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the ledger involves **Austin Riley**, whose 60.04 score sits right on the edge of our \"Strong\" tier. While he offers a favorable matchup against F. Peralta, we have to account for the 34% rain risk in the forecast and his placement in the 7-hole, which slightly suppresses his counting stat potential. He remains in the lineup because his BvP and matchup skill profile narrowly outclass the bottom-tier options. Conversely, **Jose Caballero** (42.72) is our most marginal start; his projection was battered by a -13% platoon adjustment against Jax, and he only survives the cut because our depth chart is currently thin due to the IL statuses of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**. \n\nAs we manage our daily game caps, we opted to bench the rest of our depth, including **Mickey Moniak**, who is out of the starting lineup entirely, and **Josh Naylor**, who is inactive today. We are also closely monitoring the pending status of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**; while both are currently projected for the 8-hole against K. Freeland, any movement further down the order could push them toward the \"Below floor\" category. With stolen bases at a premium, the speed profiles of **Brice Turang** and **Corbin Carroll** remain our primary engine, and we are banking on these matchups to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
